== D3: Lemma T's second sentence -- which reading, and does it need Fact 2? ==
  connected graphs n<=7 scanned: 1893731
  Fact 2 violations (residue > alpha)              : 0
  instances with s < tau                           : 0
  antecedent TRUE and s = tau  (reading (i) live)  : 0
  antecedent TRUE and s > tau  (reading (ii) live) : 139066
  -> reading (i) is VACUOUS (antecedent contradicts Lemma T's first sentence);
     reading (ii) is the only one with content, and there 'residue <= alpha-1'
     is reached from s != tau only via s >= tau, i.e. via Fact 2.

  passage under reading (ii):  residue = n - s (Lemma 1(1));
     s != tau  AND  s >= tau (Fact 2)  =>  s >= tau+1  =>  residue <= n-tau-1 = alpha-1.
     Without 's >= tau' the conclusion does not follow: s = tau-1 would give
     residue = alpha+1.  (No such graph exists -- because Fact 2 is a theorem.)

